nhtsa-vehicle pack — content licence
=====================================

This pack is derived from three US Government sources:
    NHTSA Cybersecurity Best Practices for the Safety of Modern Vehicles,
        Updated 2022 (final), 24 pages
    NHTSA Automated Driving Systems 2.0: A Vision for Safety, 2017, 36 pages
    49 CFR Part 571 (Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standards), sections 102,
        103, 105, 108, 126, 127, 135, 141, 201, 208, 209, 210, 214, 226, 301,
        and 305, as published by the eCFR versioner at date 2025-01-01
    NHTSA (US Department of Transportation)

Source licence: Public Domain (US Government work, 17 U.S.C. § 105)  (tier 1 — see
../../docs/SOURCE-VETTING.md)
No source-material download link is published (see ../../docs/LICENSING.md).

SOURCE TERMS (as carried by the sources)
----------------------------------------
All three sources are works of the U.S. Federal Government. Under 17 U.S.C.
§ 105 they are not subject to copyright protection in the United States. The
PDFs carry no separate publisher licence notice beyond that government-work
status. Use of the publications does not imply NHTSA or USDOT endorsement of
any derivative product.

OBLIGATIONS CARRIED FORWARD
---------------------------
Because the sources are U.S. Government works not subject to domestic
copyright, NO attribution, non-commercial, or share-alike obligation attaches
to them. The content of this pack may therefore be reproduced, transformed,
and redistributed freely, including commercially. As a courtesy (not an
obligation):
  - Attribution to NHTSA is provided in PACK.yaml and throughout the pack.
  - NHTSA does not endorse this pack; nothing here should be read as a NHTSA
    endorsement.
  - "NHTSA" and the publication titles are used nominatively to identify the
    sources.

THIRD-PARTY CAVEAT
------------------
This pack omits pages 8, 13, 14, and 18 of NHTSA's Cybersecurity Best Practices
for the Safety of Modern Vehicles (2022), which quote ISO/SAE 21434 requirement
text verbatim in footnotes; the omitted requirements are cited by number only.
FMVSS section text incorporates SAE, ASTM, ISO, and MIL specifications by
reference; this pack names them and reproduces none of them. Other standards
cited by name in the extracts are not reproduced.

